{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nTwelve `tests/scripts/graph` files contain 91 audited prose blocks with repetition, history, or obvious narration. Scope and behavior were revalidated against immutable commit `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`. The later `origin/main` advance to `10533b1e3f651a60e8cea5691318c108ff1f3396` does not touch these targets and is irrelevant to the citations. `test_graph_perf.py` changed since the superseded `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192` audit; the allowlist includes its new shim-absence test and post-refactor comment.\n\n## Approach and identity\nCondense only allowlisted ordinary comments and true leading docstrings. Preserve all runtime strings, prompts, fixtures, decorators, assertions, subprocess arguments, and executable behavior. Stable block IDs are `path::module-docstring`, `path::<qualified-symbol>-docstring`, or `path::<qualified-symbol>::comment(<opening words>)`; use `<module>` as the owner for module-level comments. The line spans below are immutable base citations, never the identity anchor. Adjacent blank-line cleanup is allowed only when attached to an edited block.\n\nFor each declared path, compare the immutable `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e:<path>` blob directly with the final leaf commit, even if the implementation branch is based on a later main. Parse with `type_comments=True`; remove leading docstrings only from `ast.Module`, `ast.ClassDef`, `ast.FunctionDef`, and `ast.AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; and require the remaining AST to match. This preserves runtime strings and every executable expression. Tokenize comments and compare every matched directive-bearing physical line plus any shebang byte-for-byte. The exact leaf changed-path set (`HEAD^..HEAD`) must equal the first-class `file_impact` set.\n\n## Scope — immutable base citations\n- `_helpers.py:1-7,89-93,115-119` — preserve LINK direction/storage and ARCHIVED semantics.\n- `conftest.py:1-6,31-48,69-81` — preserve parent-repository discovery isolation and graph fixture ownership.\n- `test_doctor_locks.py:1-15,36-41` — preserve live-holder informational status, stale-holder findings, and host-global snapshot-root isolation.\n- `test_doctor.py:1-8,345-356,461-472,628-639` — preserve link-before-unlink safety, rollback-anchor refresh, the non-reentrant lock rule, and continue-on-unrepairable behavior.\n- `test_graph_children_archive.py:1-6,28-33,76-89,128-139,172-189,221-233,255-259,265-278,309-321` — preserve archived filtering, transitive traversal, and redundant-edge-versus-cycle distinctions.\n- `test_graph_cycles.py:1-6,32-36,51-55,72-76,94-103,129-140,157-166,181-189,200-202,262-271,336-352,383-395,411-417` — preserve level-scoped traversal, hidden-directory exclusion, virtual/missing endpoint behavior, and accumulator termination.\n- `test_graph_hierarchy_adddep.py:1-6,29-44,88-96,112-117,161-170,206-215,247-257,301-307,361-365,427-430,438-443,487-493,513-518,546-551,591-597,625-631` — preserve structural promotion, relation grammar, quiet MCP behavior, and returned redirect records.\n- `test_graph_hierarchy_resolve.py:1-6,26-35,64-81,111-129,160-168,194-201,223-231,251-255,280-285,337-345,352,370-385,409-413,421-427,451-456,483-488,508-513,534-540` — preserve NCA-based resolution, virtual-root behavior, ancestor refusal, the non-blocking carve-out, and cycle termination.\n- `test_graph_links_push.py:1-13,26-29,37-48,63-65,106-108` — preserve LINK-before-UNLINK same-second ordering.\n- `test_graph_perf.py:1-6,35-45,75-80,107-112,118-128,165-176,194,208-219` — preserve mtime-sensitive cache invalidation, single-batch scanning, `_loader.reduce_ticket` / `_loader.reducer.reduce_all_tickets` ownership, and asserted absence of private `_reduce_ticket` / `_reducer` shims.\n- `test_graph_traversal.py:1-6,28-35,53-60,78-86,144-157,213-221,248-261,267-270` — preserve ready/blocker schema and missing/deleted tombstones as satisfied blockers.\n- `test_graph_unresolved_blocker.py:1-13,35-39` — preserve deliberate absent-target tombstone fail-open behavior.\n\nConsumers are pytest/CI and `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`; `_helpers.py` is imported across the graph suite and `conftest.py` is pytest-discovered. Graph, observability, and architecture documentation cite these contracts. No target-specific runtime docstring reader was found. Preserve `_helpers.py:182` type-ignore, `conftest.py:20` E402, `test_doctor_locks.py:70,175` no-cover pragmas, and `test_graph_perf.py:146,189,233` type-ignore directives byte-for-byte; preserve exact shebang absence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes exactly the declared `file_impact` paths and only allowlisted prose blocks or their adjacent blank lines; the immutable-base normalized-AST/runtime/directive/shebang guard passes.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and retains its listed contract and real consumers; repetition, chronology, obvious narration, and ornament are removed rather than moved.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the edits posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: stable block ID, immutable-before citation, final-commit citation (or `DELETED` plus surviving neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, `directives_exact`, before/after words, reviewer session, `semantic-preservation`, and `bloat-removal`.\n- [ ] Every TSV row records `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing rows, duplicate IDs, bad citations, or any non-PASS result block closure.\n- [ ] The focused hermetic checks, `scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and no-timeout worktree-venv `make verify` all pass. Collection-only checks never execute live Jira mutations.\n\n## Verification\nThe authoritative executable commands and DD intent are recorded in first-class `verify_commands`. Do not replace `make verify` with `make lint`, and do not put a timeout around it."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788619171222618795,"uuid":"310cb6cf-a7a7-4af7-81c0-0b0992af4e8d"}